{title: Showers of Blessing}
{artist: Daniel W. Whittle / James McGranahan}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There shall be showers of blessing
This is the [C]promise of [G]love
There shall be [G]seasons refreshing
Sent from the [D]Savior a[G]bove
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Showers of blessing, showers of blessing we [C]need
[G]Mercy-drops round us are falling
But for the [D]showers we [G]plead
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]There shall be showers of blessing
Precious re[C]viving a[G]gain
Over the [G]hills and the valleys
Sound of abun[D]dance of [G]rain
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
